# NestedText v3 — dtd rewrite ledger (audit-first, rewrite-on-findings only)
# Program: every dtd/*.dtd read whole, audited against study + house standards, rewritten only on findings; build+check+audit green per batch
# Standing rules: law numbers never reused/reordered; public entity names kept (instruments regex them); enumerations checkers read stay finite

pilot:
    file: dtd/cc-sigil.dtd (156 lines, read whole)
    verdict: HOLDS — no rewrite
    reasons:
        > Tiers S/A/B/C/D name study forms incl. claude-arguments, terraform-literal, prompt-transform-untrusted, zsh flags; 11 collisions; trust matrix bound to cc-core (LAW.SIGIL.2); ladder topics 1-10; C11 markup doctrine documented; lib/sigil.mjs measure holds both directions (LAW.SIGIL.3).
        > Deal demonstrated: audit-first means hold-when-holds; rewriting this file would be churn, not improvement.

